    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="1051" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg901"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Netherlands Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your note of the 13th instant inviting this Government to be represented at a
                    conference looking to the exemption, by means of an international agreement, of
                    hospital ships from payment of all usual port dues and taxes, to be held at The
                    Hague, in December next, between the powers signatory to The Hague convention of
                    July 29, 1899; and submitting a draft of a convention as a basis for the
                    deliberations of the proposed conference.</p>
                <p>In acknowledgment of your Government’s action, I beg leave to express my
                    appreciation and to say that the subject is receiving this Government’s
                    consideration, the result of which will be communicated to you at an early
                    date.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
